{#
  The one way this site says « déposez un fichier ici » (design.md §7.10).

  Three screens had drawn this by hand — the generic uploader, the
  gallery's album form and « Nouveau reçu » — with three paddings, two
  icons, three wordings of the same sentence, and three copies of the
  four drag listeners in JavaScript. The behaviour is now
  `public/assets/js/drop-zone.js` (`ScoutMagicDropZone.bind()`); this is
  its markup.

  An embed, not an include, so a caller can put its own controls inside:

  {% embed 'partials/drop_zone.html.twig' with {
      id: 'drop-zone',                     -- required; what the JS binds
      input_id: 'receipt-files',           -- the file input's id
      input_name: 'receipts[]',            -- omit for a JS-only picker
      accept: '.pdf,.jpg,.jpeg,.png',      -- optional
      multiple: true,                      -- optional, default false
      message: 'Glissez-déposez vos reçus ici, ou cliquez pour parcourir',
      icon: 'bi-cloud-arrow-up',           -- optional, this is the default
      size: 'lg',                          -- 'md' (default) or 'lg'
      input_label: 'Sélectionner des reçus',  -- aria-label on the input
      class_extra: 'mb-3',                 -- optional extra classes
      data: { 'upload-url': '/gallery/4/media' },  -- optional data-* on the zone
  } only %}

  Two opt-ins live in that `data` hash, both described in design.md §7.10:

      'drop-zone-for': 'photo-file'       -- the file rides the surrounding
                                             form's POST; name what was picked
      'drop-zone-preview': 'image'        -- and show a thumbnail of it

  The second is image-only and deliberately NOT derived from `accept`: a
  zone taking a PDF or a photograph of one would otherwise draw a broken
  frame for every PDF. The thumbnail is a `canvas` of the DECODED file,
  never an `img` pointed at an object URL — design.md §7.10 says why that
  distinction is not cosmetic. (Those two are named in backticks rather
  than in angle brackets on purpose: a scanner that reads this file as
  HTML sees a literal tag even inside a Twig comment, and reported the
  `img` as an image missing its alternative text.) The form around such a zone usually also
  wants `data-submit-lock` (form-submit-lock.js), which is what stops a
  second tap sending the same file twice.

  A Twig comment cannot go INSIDE the `with { … }` hash — that is Twig
  expression context, and the parser answers « Unclosed "(" ». Put it
  above the tag. (And a comment's own closing delimiter cannot appear
  inside a comment either, which is how this very paragraph broke the
  partial once.)
      {% block extra %}…{% endblock %}     -- optional, under the message
  {% endembed %}

  The input is INSIDE the zone and visually hidden: that keeps the label
  association local, and drop-zone.js opens it on a click anywhere in the
  zone. A caller whose zone carries its own <label class="btn"> controls
  passes `pick_on_click: false` to ScoutMagicDropZone.bind() instead, so
  the picker does not open twice — and overrides {% block actions %} to
  render them.

  `text-body-secondary` and the dashed border are the whole visual
  identity; drop-zone.js adds `border-primary` while a file hovers.
#}
<div id="{{ id }}"
     class="drop-zone border border-2 border-dashed rounded-3 text-center text-body-secondary
            {{ size|default('md') == 'lg' ? 'p-5' : 'p-4' }} {{ class_extra|default('') }}"
     {# The pointer only where a click actually opens something: a zone
        whose controls are its own <label>s is not itself clickable. #}
     {% if input_id is defined and input_id %}style="cursor:pointer;"{% endif %}
     {# `{%-` and the leading space, exactly as month_grid, month_day_grid,
        ai_button and the public calendar write the same loop: without a
        separator, two keys render as
        `data-drop-zone-for="x"data-drop-zone-preview="y"`, which is
        invalid markup. Browsers recover, so nothing complains — caught
        in review on the pull request for issue #756, the change that
        first passed this partial a two-key hash. #}
     {%- for key, value in data|default({}) %} data-{{ key }}="{{ value }}"{% endfor %}>
    <i class="bi {{ icon|default('bi-cloud-arrow-up') }} {{ size|default('md') == 'lg' ? 'display-4' : 'fs-2' }} d-block mb-2"
       aria-hidden="true"></i>
    {% block message %}<span>{{ message|default('') }}</span>{% endblock %}
    {% block actions %}{% endblock %}
    {# No input_id: the caller renders its own controls in {% block actions %}
       (the generic uploader offers a picker AND a camera capture, two
       inputs, each wrapped in its own <label class="btn">). #}
    {% if input_id is defined and input_id %}
        <input type="file"
               class="visually-hidden"
               id="{{ input_id }}"
               {% if input_name is defined and input_name %}name="{{ input_name }}"{% endif %}
               {% if accept is defined and accept %}accept="{{ accept }}"{% endif %}
               {% if multiple|default(false) %}multiple{% endif %}
               {% if input_label is defined and input_label %}aria-label="{{ input_label }}"{% endif %}>
    {% endif %}
    {% block extra %}{% endblock %}
</div>
